	</section>

	<section xml:id="appa-section2">
		<title>Units in This Textbook</title>

		<introduction>
			<p>Performing a dimensional analysis on some equations in this textbook can be complicated. How do we know the relationship between a farad, ohm, and second? <xref ref="appa-table-of-units-in-this-book" /> will list many properties used in this textbook, including the definition of the unit in SI base units. In <xref ref="appa-diffeq-coefficients" />, dimensional analysis of many terms that appear in differential equations (and transfer functions) will be performed. This will hopefully help for two reasons: first, to help in performing a <q>smell test</q> when deriving differential equations and transfer functions, and second, to verify that the units produced from the mathematics are accurate.</p>

			<p>Note that the radian is not defined as a base unit by SI, but is also not derived from existing base units. It will be treated as not a unit in this textbook for simplicities sake.</p>
		</introduction>

		<subsection xml:id="appa-table-of-properties">
